Wow so I'm generally not one to talk  about anything related to the personal  lives of creators of people in Hollywood  of writers directors actors whatever cuz  by and large I don't care I mean I'm not  into gossip I really truly don't care  but what's come out in WoW at the time  I'm recording this I guess about a day  ago depending on one night get this  video up it might have been a couple  days what's come out from Joss Whedon's  ex-wife in regards to things that went  on in their marriage that led to their  divorce I don't know I get the thing is  I I like so much of what Joss Whedon has  done that I feel like at least for me  for my own peace of mind I have to talk  this through and I guess you guys are  getting brought along for the ride on  this I I tend to fall very much in the  middle of the overall question and  debate of should you separate the artist  from the art and I really do treat it on  a case-by-case basis  because I think in many ways you can't  you shouldn't separate the artist from  the art because the artist is why the  art exists as it does to try and go well  look don't consider who the artist is at  all when assessing a piece of our  assumes that art exists in a vacuum but  it's not it's made by people and what  those people are and what they believe  and what they do informs their worldview  informs their creative ideas and forms  the art that they create so I I don't on  a basic level I don't believe in  separating the artists from the art I do  try and avoid condemning a piece of art  because of issues that I have with the  artist unless the issues I have have  directly seeped into the art itself so  you know that takes  buddy like HP Lovecraft who wrote some  amazing stories there's some amazing  your mythology creation you know the  entire Cthulhu Mythos n' and all that  but at the same time really really  racist guy and again part of that is a  reflection of the time he lived in and i  know there's the whole you know don't  judge by money but even for the time he  was kind of a little bit but the vast  majority of his writing that doesn't  enter into where it doesn't her into it  is awkward as heck but i think a lot of  his writing and i think a big part of  the reason why he remains as influential  as he is is the majority of sort of the  seminal pieces of his work aren't  steeped in his more egregious beliefs  that he happened to have and I also  grant these kinds of debates are a lot  easier to have when a creator when an  artist is dead because unfortunately  when they're still alive you run into  the additional issue of by supporting  this art am i financially supporting  someone who I find objectionable I'm  rambling about other artists and I guess  I'm just trying to give some some  context for my own headspace on a lot of  this so if you haven't been following so  Joss Whedon's ex-wife cakehole wrote an  I basically wrote it wrote a column  detailing basically about 15 years or so  worth of infidelity that he continually  engaged in over the course of their  marriage and that apparently he kept  from her for quite a while as well so  again I don't I don't like to delve into  you know so artists personal lives and  having an affair is very much a personal  life thing like I don't I wouldn't care  if I didn't care when it turned out that  Ben Affleck had an affair like look that  sucks that sucks for his family but I  I just I don't care so the question  becomes why why is it bothering me and  why do I feel the need to talk about  Joss Whedon having an affair or a series  of affairs as is alleged and and I don't  want to get into an argument over  whether or not what is being said is  true  the statement from Whedon side of things  is there are some inaccurate e's in her  statement but he's not outright refuting  anything directly which to me says  there's some smoke to this fire and I  don't want to linger on the on a ton on  the details of it because I don't think  they they particularly matter but the  reason that I feel the need to talk  about this is because this is a case I  think where the artists views publicly  stated views and the point of view in a  lot of his actual art is that odds with  his actions and I think cakehole herself  actually put it very well and I'm gonna  paraphrase here but she basically said  that he betrayed the very feminist  ideals that he often says that he stands  by by the fact that he forced her to be  complicit in what he was doing by not  telling her for so long so he  continually had affairs and he took away  her choice as to whether or not she  wanted to continue to be in a  relationship with someone who had issues  being faithful he did not give her that  choice he robbed her of her choice as to  whether or not she would stay with him  and try and work it out or not by not  telling her for as long as he has he  kept it all a secret and that is more  more so than just cheating you know  because cheating having an affair and I  don't want to handle wave any of that  again as uh you know oh it happens of  whatever look but the fact that he had  affairs  honestly just makes him human like many  people and again that is not me excusing  anything but that is me saying that is  not an uncommon  personal flaw when it comes to people in  Hollywood it actually is probably the  number one most common personal flaw in  terms of how early when relationships  break down but the fact that he was  apparently deceitful in it for so long  Wow and taking that choice away from  ostensibly the most important woman in  his life at the same time as he was  oftentimes kind of patting himself on  the back about how feminist he was and  how feminist his works were that becomes  a problem and it becomes a very  unfortunate one and it doesn't suddenly  make me want to like go burn my Buffy  DVD set because I do believe especially  when it comes to message material while  hypocrisy is frustrating and  disappointing and infuriating it's 