e  moment when I'm recording this I am  angrily disappointed again not because  he had an affair people in Hollywood  people the world over have affairs it  sucks it's not okay but that he would  continually and by woeful choice  live this dual life that very  deliberately undermined things that he  was putting forward not and not just I  think I think it's the thing is it's not  just in the shows like he was D would do  interviews talking about how important  strong female characterization and the  representation of strong women and  women's rights and all these other  things are to him and I'm not saying  that he's a liar and I don't think that  those things aren't important to him but  for him to push that angle so hard while  continually engaging in the behavior  that he was behaving in and very  deliberately undermining the freedom and  the choices of who was supposed to be  the most important woman in his life  yeah that's that upsets me more than  these sorts of things usually do to the  point that I actually am making a video  about it because I get normally I  wouldn't talk about this crap I don't  care but this one  there's just something frustrating about  there being a piece of art that you love  and you know that you love and when your  ability to love it becomes compromised  and that's a selfish thing I know that  because I mean the easiest way to avoid  that just stick my ears my fingers in my  ears ago to level Li and ignore the real  world and I'm not going to do that  but it's still frustrating and  infuriating and disappointing and it's  just not fun to feel that piece of art  that means something to you potentially  means a great deal to you being  tarnished by something that you have  absolutely no control over and that  sucks  and but it's worth remembering that the  tarnishment like the beauty  of the art is in the eye of the beholder  and that it can still be a force for  good and as I said I if and when the  next time I watch something made 